lib/ukfs-virtiofs: assert on the created node, not its parent

virtiofs_live_fs_create() checks the file mode of `n` — the *parent
directory* it is creating into — against S_IFREG. A directory is never a
regular file, so this fires on every single file creation:

    CRIT: [libukfs_virtiofs] <virtiofs.c @ 1332> Assertion failure:
          virtiofs_node_fmode(n) == 0100000

The node that should be checked is `newnode`, the file just created (its
attributes come back in the FUSE CREATE reply on the line above).

This makes writing a new file to a virtio-fs mount crash the guest with
assertions enabled — which is the default (LIBUKDEBUG_ENABLE_ASSERT=y) —
on any VMM, not just libkrun.

Found against unikraft 0.21.0 (Ijiraq).
--- a/lib/ukfs-virtiofs/virtiofs.c
+++ b/lib/ukfs-virtiofs/virtiofs.c
@@ -1329,7 +1329,7 @@
 
 		virtiofs_live_acquire(n);
 		virtiofs_init_node(newnode, n->dev, entry_out.nodeid, n);
-		UK_ASSERT(virtiofs_node_fmode(n) == S_IFREG);
+		UK_ASSERT(virtiofs_node_fmode(newnode) == S_IFREG);
 		virtiofs_commit_open(newnode, &open_out);
 		uk_mutex_lock(&n->dev->maplk);
 		UK_RB_INSERT(virtiofs_nodemap, &n->dev->nodemap, newnode);
